+## Findings
+
+### Bottom line
+TransDigm’s earnings support debt service, but its October distribution materially reduces retained creditor protection; year-end liquidity must not be interpreted as cash available after shareholder payments. Reported EBITDA and cash interest provide a firmer debt-service baseline than the more generous issuer-adjusted measure.
+Basis: TDG_2024-09-30_10-K_0001260221-24-000083_tdg-20240930.htm.jsonl, pages 54–56; TDG_2024-09-30_10-K_0001260221-24-000083_tdg-20240930.htm.jsonl, page 71; TDG_2024-09-30_10-K_0001260221-24-000083_tdg-20240930.htm.jsonl, page 123
+
+Gross leverage is 6.53x and cash-interest cover is 3.29x on reported EBITDA. Reported net leverage of 4.88x becomes 6.02x after the October 2024 special-dividend and dividend-equivalent payments, holding annual EBITDA unchanged. Strong cash generation is the principal counterweight, but the distribution demonstrates that earnings growth need not translate into durable deleveraging.
+Basis: calculation C02; calculation C08; calculation C09; calculation C10; calculation C11; calculation C12; TDG_2024-09-30_10-K_0001260221-24-000083_tdg-20240930.htm.jsonl, page 170
